00:27:17.690 --> 00:27:20.558
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:27:22.470 --> 00:27:25.038
How many different ways can
you run a container on GCP?

00:27:25.038 --> 00:27:25.830
AJA HAMMERLY: Yeah.

00:27:25.830 --> 00:27:27.570
I love this question, Jon.

00:27:27.570 --> 00:27:29.490
I think we did it
a previous time

00:27:29.490 --> 00:27:32.610
that I was on the podcast a year
or probably more than a year

00:27:32.610 --> 00:27:35.130
ago, but the answer has changed.

00:27:35.130 --> 00:27:35.880
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC]

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:38.490
So by my count, there
are at least five ways

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.320
to run a container on GCP.

00:27:40.320 --> 00:27:43.180
The obvious one, Google
Kubernetes Engine, GKE.

00:27:43.180 --> 00:27:44.108
[PING]

00:27:44.108 --> 00:27:45.275
Also, now we have Cloud Run,

00:27:45.275 --> 00:27:45.810
[PING]

00:27:45.810 --> 00:27:47.870
which is another way
of running containers.

00:27:47.870 --> 00:27:49.780
But there are a couple of ways
most people don't know about.

00:27:49.780 --> 00:27:51.655
First of all, App Engine
Flexible Environment

00:27:51.655 --> 00:27:53.190
can actually run a container.

00:27:53.190 --> 00:27:54.160
[PING]

00:27:54.160 --> 00:27:55.600
It's based around containers.

00:27:55.600 --> 00:27:58.260
And so if you have a
container, that is an option.

00:27:58.260 --> 00:27:59.100
And Compute Engine--

00:27:59.100 --> 00:27:59.600
[PING]

00:27:59.600 --> 00:28:01.500
--and this is the one that even
a lot of Googlers don't know

00:28:01.500 --> 00:28:02.250
about--

00:28:02.250 --> 00:28:04.380
can actually start
a Compute Engine VM

00:28:04.380 --> 00:28:05.950
from a container image.

00:28:05.950 --> 00:28:07.770
And then the fifth
one is you can always

00:28:07.770 --> 00:28:10.980
use a VM as a computer and set
up your own either Kubernetes

00:28:10.980 --> 00:28:12.870
environment or
Docker environment

00:28:12.870 --> 00:28:15.060
to run a container,
that way not using

00:28:15.060 --> 00:28:16.420
any of the managed services.

00:28:16.420 --> 00:28:17.090
[PING]

00:28:17.090 --> 00:28:19.770
So at my best count, there
are at least five ways

00:28:19.770 --> 00:28:21.277
to run a container on GCP.

00:28:21.277 --> 00:28:22.360
JON FOUST: That's awesome.

00:28:22.360 --> 00:28:25.650
And it's kind of interesting
to see the evolution of GCP

00:28:25.650 --> 00:28:27.860
and how it supports containers
because how many ways

00:28:27.860 --> 00:28:29.610
were there about a
year ago would you say?

00:28:29.610 --> 00:28:32.360
AJA HAMMERLY: At my entire
time at Google, pretty much

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:33.480
we've had four.

00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:34.710
Cloud Run is the new one.

00:28:34.710 --> 00:28:37.200
And Cloud Run is
cool and awesome,

00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:39.198
and folks should
go check it out.

00:28:39.198 --> 00:28:39.990
JON FOUST: Awesome.

